; S004 FVG -- shadow (parity) pass in the Strategy Tester. ALGODEV-62 phase D.
;
; What this preset is for: run the EA over broker history with the order layer
; switched OFF, so the engine, the Asia-window filter and the portfolio-wide
; daily cap all run and get written to <strategy>_trades.csv, but nothing is
; ever sent to the market. mt5/tools/s004_parity.py then diffs that file
; against strategies/fvg_mtf.py re-run on the same bars.
;
; InpTradeEnabled=false is the whole point -- do not flip it here.
;
; The account guard is off, like in live: it is off by DESIGN, not just for the
; test (see the note in S004_FVG.mq5 and backtest/run_s004_guard_modes.py). A
; halt is also a live-only decision the backtest knows nothing about, so it
; would show up as `ea_halted` rows in the parity report.
;
; InpServerTzRule must be the BROKER's rule, not the strategy's. S004 decides on
; its own EET/EEST clock with EUROPEAN DST dates; the runtime converts. Most
; prop servers are EET with US DST (=2) -- check the EA's `init` event, it logs
; the observed offset. Getting this wrong moves the Asia window by an hour for
; the weeks the two DST calendars disagree.
;
; Enum codes: ServerTzRule/DayResetRule 0=UTC 1=FIXED 2=EET_US_DST 3=EET_EU_DST 4=CET_EU_DST
InpRiskPct=1.0
InpMaxTradesPerDay=2
InpInitialBalance=10000.0
InpDailyGuardPct=0.0
InpMaxGuardPct=0.0
InpDayResetRule=1
InpDayResetFixedHours=3
InpServerTzRule=2
InpServerFixedHours=0
InpMagic=4004
InpWarmupBars=1000
InpTradeEnabled=false
InpWriteTradesCsv=true
InpLogToCommon=true
InpTimerSeconds=60
